        <h2 id="early">Early-exit modes</h2>

        <pre><code>pkgbuild -g example
pkgbuild -o example
pkgbuild -x example
pkgbuild -p example
pkgbuild -C example</code></pre>

        <p>
            These modes stop after checksum generation, source download,
            extraction, manifest generation, or cleanup. They are useful for
            inspecting a port without running its full build.
        </p>

        <h2 id="pipeline">Execution pipeline</h2>

        <ol>
            <li>Load the configuration and resolve source, package, work, and build-state directories.</li>
            <li>Resolve the job count and export parallelism for Make, Ninja, CMake, Cargo, and Go.</li>
            <li>Validate the port recipe and its required metadata.</li>
            <li>Handle any early-exit option.</li>
            <li>Create a per-package lock and fetch the declared sources.</li>
            <li>Verify checksums, prepare the source workspace, and extract archives.</li>
            <li>Run the optional recipe preparation step and the recipe's build function.</li>
            <li>Assemble the staged result, apply package policy, compress it, and write its file list.</li>

            <li>
                Remove the workspace unless <code>--keep-work</code> was requested.
            </li>

            <li>
                Install the resulting archive when <code>--install</code>,
                <code>--upgrade</code>, or <code>--reinstall</code> was selected.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="outputs">Outputs and failure behavior</h2>

        <p>
            The archive name is
            <code>name-version-release.epkg.tar.&lt;gz|bz2|xz|lz4|zstd&gt;</code>.
            The command uses a lock to prevent two builds of the same package
            from sharing one workspace. An interrupted build removes the lock
            and follows the normal cleanup path.
        </p>

        <p>
            For the recipe fields, source naming, checksums, staging rules,
            persistent build helpers, pruning policy, and review checklist, use
            the dedicated <a href="#/pm/ports">Creating ports</a> manual.
        </p>

        <h2 id="help">
            <code>pkgbuild help</code>
        </h2>

        <pre><code>Usage:
    pkgbuild &lt;options&gt; [&lt;arg&gt;]

Options:
    -q  --quiet            show only status messages and errors
    -i, --install          install package into system
    -u, --upgrade          upgrade package
    -r, --reinstall        reinstall package
    -c, --ignore-conflict  ignore conflict when installing package
    -v, --verbose          verbose install process
    -f, --force-rebuild    rebuild package
    -m, --skip-checksum    skip checksum checking
    -g, --gen-checksum     generate checksum
    -o, --download         download only source file
    -x, --extract          extract only source file
    -p, --pkgfiles         generate list files in package
    -w, --keep-work        keep working directory
    -h, --help             show this help message
    -C, --clean            remove downloaded sources and prebuilt packages

Global options:
    --config=&lt;config&gt;      use custom config file
    --srcdir=&lt;path&gt;        override directory path for sources
    --pkgdir=&lt;path&gt;        override directory path for compiled package
    --workdir=&lt;path&gt;       override directory path for working dir
    --jobs=&lt;N&gt;             override parallel build jobs (default: JOBS in config, or nproc)
    --no-backup            skip backup configuration file when upgrading package</code></pre>
